      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) in the given diagram, we need to use the fact that the sum of the angles around a point is \\( 360^\\circ \\). The angles given in the diagram are \\( 4x^\\circ \\), \\( 5x^\\circ \\), \\( 2x^\\circ \\), and \\( x^\\circ \\), and these angles form a complete circle around a point.\n\nWe can set up the equation as follows:\n\\[\n4x + 5x + 2x + x = 360\n\\]\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\\[\n12x = 360\n\\]\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 12:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{360}{12} = 30\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{30}\\).\n\nTo verify, we can substitute \\( x = 30 \\) back into the original angles:\n\\[\n4x = 4 \\times 30 = 120^\\circ, \\quad 5x = 5 \\times 30 = 150^\\circ, \\quad 2x = 2 \\times 30 = 60^\\circ, \\quad x = 30^\\circ\n\\]\nThe sum of these angles is:\n\\[\n120^\\circ + 150^\\circ + 60^\\circ + 30^\\circ = 360^\\circ\n\\]\nThis confirms that our solution is correct. The value of \\( x \\) is indeed \\(\\boxed{30}\\).",
